      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "The `kubernetes.io/cluster-service: \"true\"` label is sprinkled across over 100 yaml files in the kubernetes repo (according to github search). However, I could not find any documentation around the effect of this label.\r\n\r\nAfter searching the code base, it seems that:\r\n1. The label was being used by the addon manager in the past, but it has since been deprecated.\r\n2. The `kubectl cluster-info` command seems to be the only place where this label is used in the code. It is used to display the addresses of the services that contain this label.\r\n\r\nWould it make sense to document this label, and also cleanup the instances of this label that exist on manifests that are not `kind: Service`?\r\n\r\n/kind cleanup\r\n/kind docs",
